10	--- /dev/null
11	+++ b/packages/database/features/spaceTableAccess.feature
12	@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
13	+Feature: Space table access
14	+  User story:
15	+  * As a user of a plugin
16	+  * Logged in through a given space's anonymous account
17	+  * I want to read the spaces I can reach, with their grants and member accounts, and to manage the spaces I edit
18	+  * And no other user should be able to change them without editor access
19	+
20	+  Acceptance criteria:
21	+  * Space returns every space where I have partial access or more
22	+  * SpaceAccess and LocalAccess return the rows of every space where I have reader access or more
23	+  * Editor access to a space allows updating and deleting it, and writing its grants
24	+  * Anyone signed in can create a space
25	+
26	+  Background:
27	+    Given the database is blank
28	+    And the user user1 opens the Roam plugin in space s1
29	+    And the user user2 opens the Roam plugin in space s2
30	+    And the user user3 opens the Roam plugin in space s3
31	+    And user of space s1 creates group g1
32	+    And user of space s1 adds space s2 to group g1
33	+
34	+  Scenario: Without a grant, a space sees only itself
35	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should see these rows per space:
36	+      | table       | space | count |
37	+      | Space       | s2    | 1     |
38	+      | SpaceAccess | s2    | 1     |
39	+      | LocalAccess | s2    | 1     |
40	+
41	+  Scenario: Reader access shows the space, its grants and its members
42	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
43	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
44	+      | g1           | s1        | reader      |
45	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should see these rows per space:
46	+      | table       | space | count |
47	+      | Space       | s1    | 1     |
48	+      | Space       | s2    | 1     |
49	+      | SpaceAccess | s1    | 2     |
50	+      | SpaceAccess | s2    | 1     |
51	+      | LocalAccess | s1    | 1     |
52	+      | LocalAccess | s2    | 1     |
53	+    And a user logged in space s3 should see these rows per space:
54	+      | table       | space | count |
55	+      | Space       | s3    | 1     |
56	+      | SpaceAccess | s3    | 1     |
57	+      | LocalAccess | s3    | 1     |
58	+
59	+  Scenario: Partial access shows the space, but not its grants or members
60	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
61	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
62	+      | g1           | s1        | partial     |
63	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should see these rows per space:
64	+      | table       | space | count |
65	+      | Space       | s1    | 1     |
66	+      | Space       | s2    | 1     |
67	+      | SpaceAccess | s2    | 1     |
68	+      | LocalAccess | s2    | 1     |
69	+
70	+  Scenario: Editor access shows the space, its grants and its members
71	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
72	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
73	+      | g1           | s1        | editor      |
74	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should see these rows per space:
75	+      | table       | space | count |
76	+      | Space       | s1    | 1     |
77	+      | Space       | s2    | 1     |
78	+      | SpaceAccess | s1    | 2     |
79	+      | SpaceAccess | s2    | 1     |
80	+      | LocalAccess | s1    | 1     |
81	+      | LocalAccess | s2    | 1     |
82	+
83	+  Scenario: A space can write its own grants
84	+    Then a user logged in space s1 should get these write results in space s1:
85	+      | table       | insert  | update  | delete  |
86	+      | SpaceAccess | allowed | allowed | allowed |
87	+
88	+  Scenario: A space can update and delete itself
89	+    Then a user logged in space s1 should get these write results in space s1:
90	+      | table | insert  | update  | delete  |
91	+      | Space | allowed | allowed | allowed |
92	+
93	+  Scenario: Without a grant, another space can only create spaces
94	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
95	+      | table       | insert  | update | delete |
96	+      | SpaceAccess | denied  | denied | denied |
97	+      | Space       | allowed | denied | denied |
98	+
99	+  Scenario: Reader access does not allow writes to the space or its grants
100	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
101	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
102	+      | g1           | s1        | reader      |
103	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
104	+      | table       | insert  | update | delete |
105	+      | SpaceAccess | denied  | denied | denied |
106	+      | Space       | allowed | denied | denied |
107	+
108	+  Scenario: Partial access does not allow writes to the space or its grants
109	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
110	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
111	+      | g1           | s1        | partial     |
112	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
113	+      | table       | insert  | update | delete |
114	+      | SpaceAccess | denied  | denied | denied |
115	+      | Space       | allowed | denied | denied |
116	+
117	+  Scenario: Editor access allows writing the space's grants
118	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
119	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
120	+      | g1           | s1        | editor      |
121	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
122	+      | table       | insert  | update  | delete  |
123	+      | SpaceAccess | allowed | allowed | allowed |
124	+
125	+  Scenario: Editor access allows updating and deleting the space
126	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
127	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
128	+      | g1           | s1        | editor      |
129	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
130	+      | table | insert  | update  | delete  |
131	+      | Space | allowed | allowed | allowed |
