675	+Feature: Table write access
676	+  User story:
677	+  * As a user of a plugin
678	+  * Logged in through a given space's anonymous account
679	+  * I want to write the concepts, documents, contents, file references and resource grants of spaces I edit
680	+  * And no other user should be able to write them without editor access
681	+
682	+  Acceptance criteria:
683	+  * Editor access to a space allows inserting, updating and deleting its rows
684	+  * Reader or partial access to a space allows no writes
685	+  * A user can delete a resource grant made to them, even without editor access
686	+
687	+  Background:
688	+    Given the database is blank
689	+    And the user user1 opens the Roam plugin in space s1
690	+    And the user user2 opens the Roam plugin in space s2
691	+    And Concept are added to the database:
692	+      | $id | name    | _space_id | _author_id | source_local_id | created    | last_modified | @is_schema | @literal_content | @reference_content |
693	+      | n1  | claim 1 | s1        | user1      | ln1             | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    | true       | {}               | {}                 |
694	+      | n2  | claim 2 | s1        | user1      | ln2             | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    | true       | {}               | {}                 |
695	+    And Document are added to the database:
696	+      | $id | _space_id | _author_id | source_local_id | created    | last_modified |
697	+      | d1  | s1        | user1      | ln1             | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    |
698	+      | d2  | s1        | user1      | ln2             | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    |
699	+    And Content are added to the database:
700	+      | $id | _document_id | _space_id | _author_id | source_local_id | variant | scale    | text    | created    | last_modified |
701	+      | c1f | d1           | s1        | user1      | ln1             | full    | document | claim 1 | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    |
702	+      | c2f | d2           | s1        | user1      | ln2             | full    | document | claim 2 | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    |
703	+    And FileReference are added to the database:
704	+      | _space_id | source_local_id | filepath | filehash | created    | last_modified |
705	+      | s1        | ln1             | one.png  | h1       | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    |
706	+      | s1        | ln2             | two.png  | h2       | 2025/01/01 | 2025/01/01    |
707	+    And user of space s1 creates group g1
708	+    And user of space s1 adds space s2 to group g1
709	+
710	+  Scenario: A space can write its own rows
711	+    Then a user logged in space s1 should get these write results in space s1:
712	+      | table          | insert  | update  | delete  |
713	+      | FileReference  | allowed | allowed | allowed |
714	+      | Content        | allowed | allowed | allowed |
715	+      | Document       | allowed | allowed | allowed |
716	+      | Concept        | allowed | allowed | allowed |
717	+      | ResourceAccess | allowed | allowed | allowed |
718	+
719	+  Scenario: Without a grant, another space cannot write
720	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
721	+      | table          | insert | update | delete |
722	+      | FileReference  | denied | denied | denied |
723	+      | Content        | denied | denied | denied |
724	+      | Document       | denied | denied | denied |
725	+      | Concept        | denied | denied | denied |
726	+      | ResourceAccess | denied | denied | denied |
727	+
728	+  Scenario: Reader access does not allow writes
729	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
730	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
731	+      | g1           | s1        | reader      |
732	+    # A grant to a group the reader is not in: visible through reader access, but not the reader's to delete.
733	+    And user of space s1 creates group g2
734	+    And ResourceAccess are added to the database:
735	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | source_local_id |
736	+      | g2           | s1        | ln1             |
737	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
738	+      | table          | insert | update | delete |
739	+      | FileReference  | denied | denied | denied |
740	+      | Content        | denied | denied | denied |
741	+      | Document       | denied | denied | denied |
742	+      | Concept        | denied | denied | denied |
743	+      | ResourceAccess | denied | denied | denied |
744	+
745	+  Scenario: Partial access allows only deleting a grant made to the user
746	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
747	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
748	+      | g1           | s1        | partial     |
749	+    And ResourceAccess are added to the database:
750	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | source_local_id |
751	+      | g1           | s1        | ln1             |
752	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
753	+      | table          | insert | update | delete  |
754	+      | FileReference  | denied | denied | denied  |
755	+      | Content        | denied | denied | denied  |
756	+      | Document       | denied | denied | denied  |
757	+      | Concept        | denied | denied | denied  |
758	+      | ResourceAccess | denied | denied | allowed |
759	+
760	+  Scenario: Editor access allows writes
761	+    When SpaceAccess are added to the database:
762	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
763	+      | g1           | s1        | editor      |
764	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
765	+      | table          | insert  | update  | delete  |
766	+      | FileReference  | allowed | allowed | allowed |
767	+      | Content        | allowed | allowed | allowed |
768	+      | Document       | allowed | allowed | allowed |
769	+      | Concept        | allowed | allowed | allowed |
770	+      | ResourceAccess | allowed | allowed | allowed |
771	+
772	+  # The grant belongs to a group the writer isn't in, so only the editor branch of the delete policy can remove it.
773	+  Scenario: An editor can delete a resource grant made to someone else
774	+    Given the user user3 opens the Roam plugin in space s3
775	+    And user of space s3 creates group g2
776	+    And SpaceAccess are added to the database:
777	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | permissions |
778	+      | g1           | s1        | editor      |
779	+    And ResourceAccess are added to the database:
780	+      | _account_uid | _space_id | source_local_id |
781	+      | g2           | s1        | ln1             |
782	+    Then a user logged in space s2 should get these write results in space s1:
783	+      | table          | insert  | update  | delete  |
784	+      | ResourceAccess | allowed | allowed | allowed |
785	+    And the database should contain 0 ResourceAccess
